      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63322",
      ":question/problem": "Debbie recorded the heights of her gymnastics teammates and found that the girls have a mean height of $163cm$; the height of each girl is given below:\n$158cm, 161cm, 162cm, 166cm, 168cm$\n\nThe mean absolute deviation (MAD) her male teammates' heights was $2.5cm$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The MAD for the girls' heights is $3.2cm$.\n2. A comparison of the MADs suggests the girls' heights have the same spread as boys'.\n3. A comparison of the MADs suggests the girls' heights have a larger spread than boys'."
